      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "In Utah, the average cost for a full residential roof replacement typically runs between $8,500 and $18,000. For a standard 2,000 sq. ft. single-family home with architectural shingles, most homeowners pay around $10,000 to $16,000 , though costs can vary widely depending on the materials used, the pitch of your roof, and local labor rates.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
